      "markdownBody": "# CodeRabbit findings for PAN-5236 (PR #5251)\n\nCodeRabbit posted 3 inline finding(s). CodeRabbit is advisory: nothing waits for these,\nbut each one gets an answer, either a fix or a reply with your reason.\n\n- Thread 4571757572 · src/dashboard/frontend/src/lib/buildDrift.ts:87 [Minor]: Record a pending check when a rising edge arrives during an active check.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5251#discussion_r4571757572\n- Thread 4571757578 · src/dashboard/frontend/tests/pan-5236-new-build-banner.spec.ts:56 [Minor]: Wait for the drift check before asserting banner absence.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5251#discussion_r4571757578\n- Thread 4571757584 · src/dashboard/frontend/tests/pan-5236-new-build-banner.spec.ts:112 [Minor]: Do not restore the draft during the reload under test.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5251#discussion_r4571757584\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Read each thread (open its link, or the code at the path and line).\n2. If you agree with a finding, fix it.\n3. If you reject a finding, reply on its thread with your reason:\n   `gh api repos/eltmon/overdeck/pulls/5251/comments/<thread id>/replies -f body=\"<reason>\"`\n4. If you changed code: run the quality gates on what you touched, commit, push, then run `pan review request PAN-5236 -m \"CodeRabbit <thread ids>: <what you changed>\"`.\n   If you only replied, you are done.\n5. If PR #5251 has already merged when you read this, stop: after the merge Overdeck files a follow-up issue\n   for every thread with no reply, no later commit to its file, and no re-review request naming its thread id."
